1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,014
Sweetheart, my best friend Evelyn owned forty-two

2
00:00:04,014 --> 00:00:05,735
bakeries across Ohio.

3
00:00:05,915 --> 00:00:07,936
She was worth more money than this

4
00:00:07,936 --> 00:00:09,363
whole town put together.

5
00:00:09,543 --> 00:00:11,886
And two weeks before Christmas,

6
00:00:11,886 --> 00:00:13,926
I watched her put on a torn

7
00:00:13,926 --> 00:00:16,495
coat from the church rummage sale,

8
00:00:16,495 --> 00:00:18,611
rub coal dust on her cheeks,

9
00:00:18,611 --> 00:00:21,634
and walk into the fanciest restaurant in

10
00:00:21,634 --> 00:00:24,657
Columbus looking like a woman who hadn't

11
00:00:24,657 --> 00:00:26,168
eaten in three days.

12
00:00:26,519 --> 00:00:28,450
She was going to meet the girl

13
00:00:28,450 --> 00:00:30,640
her only grandson wanted to marry.

14
00:00:30,820 --> 00:00:33,430
And the girl had no idea who

15
00:00:33,430 --> 00:00:34,175
she was.

16
00:00:34,355 --> 00:00:36,634
Tonight I'm going to tell you exactly

17
00:00:36,634 --> 00:00:38,359
what happened at that table,

18
00:00:38,359 --> 00:00:40,577
what the bride said when she thought

19
00:00:40,577 --> 00:00:42,486
nobody important was listening,

20
00:00:42,486 --> 00:00:44,703
and the surprise at the wedding that

21
00:00:44,703 --> 00:00:46,859
made three hundred people stand up.

22
00:00:47,039 --> 00:00:48,169
Stay with me,

23
00:00:48,169 --> 00:00:52,078
honey, because nobody saw that ending coming.

24
00:00:52,258 --> 00:00:53,558
Not even me.

25
00:00:53,909 --> 00:00:56,301
Evelyn and I grew up two houses

26
00:00:56,301 --> 00:00:57,844
apart on Elm Street.

27
00:00:58,024 --> 00:01:00,822
Her family was even poorer than mine.

28
00:01:01,002 --> 00:01:03,690
Her father left when she was six,

29
00:01:03,690 --> 00:01:06,134
and her mother cleaned houses.

30
00:01:06,314 --> 00:01:07,993
In nineteen sixty-one,

31
00:01:07,993 --> 00:01:11,198
with eighty dollars and her mother's bread

32
00:01:11,198 --> 00:01:14,251
recipe, Evelyn opened a little bakery on

33
00:01:14,251 --> 00:01:16,159
Main Street in Mansfield.

34
00:01:16,339 --> 00:01:18,194
By the time she was fifty,

35
00:01:18,194 --> 00:01:20,263
there were forty-two of them.

36
00:01:20,614 --> 00:01:22,493
But she never changed,

37
00:01:22,493 --> 00:01:23,005
honey.

38
00:01:23,185 --> 00:01:25,438
She drove a twelve-year-old Buick.

39
00:01:25,618 --> 00:01:27,336
She clipped coupons.

40
00:01:27,516 --> 00:01:29,733
She bought her dresses at Sears.

41
00:01:29,913 --> 00:01:31,346
And she always said,

42
00:01:31,346 --> 00:01:34,282
Ruthie, money shows you who people really

43
00:01:34,282 --> 00:01:34,569
are.

44
00:01:34,749 --> 00:01:36,846
Most people never find out,

45
00:01:36,846 --> 00:01:39,021
because they never have any.

46
00:01:39,201 --> 00:01:41,593
I find out every single day.

47
00:01:41,773 --> 00:01:43,816
That's what money did to her.

48
00:01:43,996 --> 00:01:46,867
It made her suspicious of everybody who

49
00:01:46,867 --> 00:01:47,897
smiled at her.

50
00:01:48,248 --> 00:01:50,535
Her only grandson was Michael.

51
00:01:50,715 --> 00:01:53,390
His parents died in a car accident

52
00:01:53,390 --> 00:01:54,728
when he was nine,

53
00:01:54,728 --> 00:01:57,089
and Evelyn raised him herself.

54
00:01:57,269 --> 00:01:58,734
He was a good boy,

55
00:01:58,734 --> 00:02:00,363
sweetheart, a quiet,

56
00:02:00,363 --> 00:02:03,457
gentle boy who became a schoolteacher.

57
00:02:03,637 --> 00:02:05,921
And in the fall of two thousand

58
00:02:05,921 --> 00:02:08,499
three, he brought home a girl named

59
00:02:08,499 --> 00:02:10,562
Brittany, beautiful, blonde,

60
00:02:10,562 --> 00:02:13,215
from a wealthy family in Cincinnati.

61
00:02:13,395 --> 00:02:16,077
And they were engaged by Thanksgiving.

62
00:02:16,427 --> 00:02:19,306
Michael had never told Brittany about his

63
00:02:19,306 --> 00:02:20,711
grandmother's money.

64
00:02:20,891 --> 00:02:23,242
Evelyn had asked him not to,

65
00:02:23,242 --> 00:02:24,838
since he was a boy.

66
00:02:25,018 --> 00:02:26,924
As far as Brittany knew,

67
00:02:26,924 --> 00:02:28,671
Michael was a teacher,

68
00:02:28,671 --> 00:02:31,292
raised by a grandma who worked at

69
00:02:31,292 --> 00:02:32,007
a bakery.

70
00:02:32,187 --> 00:02:34,405
And something bothered Evelyn.

71
00:02:34,585 --> 00:02:36,874
Brittany had been sweet as pie to

72
00:02:36,874 --> 00:02:39,788
Michael's face, but Evelyn had noticed how

73
00:02:39,788 --> 00:02:41,800
she looked at his old car and

74
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:43,257
his little apartment.

75
00:02:43,608 --> 00:02:45,693
So one night in December,

76
00:02:45,693 --> 00:02:48,529
Evelyn sat at my kitchen table and

77
00:02:48,529 --> 00:02:49,947
told me her plan.

78
00:02:50,127 --> 00:02:51,725
I said, Evelyn,

79
00:02:51,725 --> 00:02:53,110
that's crazy.

80
00:02:53,290 --> 00:02:55,707
That's a terrible trick to play on

81
00:02:55,707 --> 00:02:56,204
a girl.

82
00:02:56,384 --> 00:02:57,381
And she said,

83
00:02:57,381 --> 00:03:00,065
Ruthie, I'm seventy-nine years old.

84
00:03:00,245 --> 00:03:01,224
When I die,

85
00:03:01,224 --> 00:03:03,449
that boy gets everything.

86
00:03:03,629 --> 00:03:06,149
Forty-two bakeries and every penny.

87
00:03:06,329 --> 00:03:08,569
I have to know who he's marrying.

88
00:03:08,749 --> 00:03:10,677
And I need you to help me.

89
00:03:10,857 --> 00:03:13,284
In a minute I'll tell you what

90
00:03:13,284 --> 00:03:14,255
my part was,

91
00:03:14,255 --> 00:03:16,278
and why I almost said no.

92
00:03:16,629 --> 00:03:19,428
Michael was taking Brittany to dinner at

93
00:03:19,428 --> 00:03:22,927
the Fairmont, the fanciest restaurant in Columbus,

94
00:03:22,927 --> 00:03:24,117
for her birthday.

95
00:03:24,297 --> 00:03:26,259
He'd saved for two months.

96
00:03:26,439 --> 00:03:29,198
Evelyn would come in from the street,

97
00:03:29,198 --> 00:03:31,287
dressed as a poor old woman,

98
00:03:31,287 --> 00:03:33,151
and ask to sit down for a

99
00:03:33,151 --> 00:03:35,239
minute because she was cold.

100
00:03:35,419 --> 00:03:37,997
She'd pretend she didn't know Michael.

101
00:03:38,177 --> 00:03:40,162
And my job was to sit at

102
00:03:40,162 --> 00:03:43,552
the next table and watch Brittany's face.

103
00:03:43,903 --> 00:03:45,916
And Michael was in on it,

104
00:03:45,916 --> 00:03:46,399
honey.

105
00:03:46,579 --> 00:03:47,518
He hated it,

106
00:03:47,518 --> 00:03:49,790
but he loved his grandmother,

107
00:03:49,790 --> 00:03:50,886
and he agreed.

108
00:03:51,066 --> 00:03:52,969
He said, Grandma,

109
00:03:52,969 --> 00:03:54,201
you'll see.

110
00:03:54,381 --> 00:03:55,762
She's wonderful.

111
00:03:55,942 --> 00:03:57,417
You'll feel terrible.

112
00:03:57,597 --> 00:03:59,243
And Evelyn said,

113
00:03:59,243 --> 00:04:00,273
I hope so,

114
00:04:00,273 --> 00:04:01,405
sweetheart.

115
00:04:01,585 --> 00:04:03,291
I truly hope so.

116
00:04:03,471 --> 00:04:05,894
I've never wanted to be wrong so

117
00:04:05,894 --> 00:04:07,105
much in my life.

118
00:04:07,456 --> 00:04:10,997
That night, it was sleeting in Columbus.

119
00:04:11,177 --> 00:04:12,914
I sat at a little table by

120
00:04:12,914 --> 00:04:14,986
the window with a cup of coffee

121
00:04:14,986 --> 00:04:16,122
I couldn't drink.

122
00:04:16,302 --> 00:04:17,560
At seven fifteen,

123
00:04:17,560 --> 00:04:20,446
Michael and Brittany were seated at the

124
00:04:20,446 --> 00:04:21,260
next table.

125
00:04:21,440 --> 00:04:23,488
She was in a white dress with

126
00:04:23,488 --> 00:04:24,336
a fur stole,

127
00:04:24,336 --> 00:04:26,808
and she complained about the table,

128
00:04:26,808 --> 00:04:27,868
then the bread,

129
00:04:27,868 --> 00:04:28,998
then the waiter.

130
00:04:29,178 --> 00:04:32,278
Michael just smiled and held her hand.

131
00:04:32,628 --> 00:04:35,305
If you're enjoying Grandma's story,

132
00:04:35,305 --> 00:04:37,370
tap the like button for me,

133
00:04:37,370 --> 00:04:38,212
sweetheart.

134
00:04:38,392 --> 00:04:41,608
It helps more people find these stories.

135
00:04:41,788 --> 00:04:43,113
At seven thirty,

136
00:04:43,113 --> 00:04:44,935
the front door opened,

137
00:04:44,935 --> 00:04:46,922
and a cold wind came in,

138
00:04:46,922 --> 00:04:48,661
and Evelyn walked in.

139
00:04:48,841 --> 00:04:51,883
I almost didn't recognize her myself.

140
00:04:52,063 --> 00:04:53,584
Torn brown coat.

141
00:04:53,764 --> 00:04:55,993
A scarf over her hair.

142
00:04:56,173 --> 00:04:58,669
Old men's boots soaked through.

143
00:04:58,849 --> 00:05:01,214
She shuffled right up to their table

144
00:05:01,214 --> 00:05:03,120
and put a shaking hand on the

145
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:04,631
back of an empty chair.

146
00:05:04,981 --> 00:05:07,390
She said, very quietly,

147
00:05:07,390 --> 00:05:09,903
excuse me, young people.

148
00:05:10,083 --> 00:05:11,476
I'm so sorry.

149
00:05:11,656 --> 00:05:13,932
It's very cold outside.

150
00:05:14,112 --> 00:05:16,396
Could an old woman sit down for

151
00:05:16,396 --> 00:05:18,384
just a minute and get warm?

152
00:05:18,564 --> 00:05:19,830
I won't bother you.

153
00:05:20,010 --> 00:05:22,147
Michael started to stand up,

154
00:05:22,147 --> 00:05:24,055
the way he'd been raised,

155
00:05:24,055 --> 00:05:25,734
to pull out the chair.

156
00:05:25,914 --> 00:05:28,318
And Brittany put her hand flat on

157
00:05:28,318 --> 00:05:30,722
his arm, and pushed him back down

158
00:05:30,722 --> 00:05:31,742
into his seat.

159
00:05:32,092 --> 00:05:35,459
Brittany didn't even look at Evelyn's face.

160
00:05:35,639 --> 00:05:37,322
She looked at the boots,

161
00:05:37,322 --> 00:05:38,936
dripping on the carpet.

162
00:05:39,116 --> 00:05:40,158
And she said,

163
00:05:40,158 --> 00:05:43,125
loud enough for the next three tables

164
00:05:43,125 --> 00:05:45,130
to hear, are you serious?

165
00:05:45,310 --> 00:05:46,749
This is a private dinner.

166
00:05:46,929 --> 00:05:49,445
Then she waved at the waiter and

167
00:05:49,445 --> 00:05:50,702
said, excuse me,

168
00:05:50,702 --> 00:05:53,375
can somebody get this woman out of

169
00:05:53,375 --> 00:05:53,768
here?

170
00:05:53,948 --> 00:05:56,105
She's dripping on everything,

171
00:05:56,105 --> 00:05:57,222
and she smells.

172
00:05:57,572 --> 00:05:59,354
Evelyn didn't move,

173
00:05:59,354 --> 00:05:59,917
honey.

174
00:06:00,097 --> 00:06:02,422
She said, just a minute,

175
00:06:02,422 --> 00:06:02,906
dear.

176
00:06:03,086 --> 00:06:04,793
My feet are frozen.

177
00:06:04,973 --> 00:06:06,471
And Brittany laughed.

178
00:06:06,651 --> 00:06:08,106
She actually laughed,

179
00:06:08,106 --> 00:06:09,769
and she said to Michael,

180
00:06:09,769 --> 00:06:11,502
this is why I told you we

181
00:06:11,502 --> 00:06:13,373
should've gone to the club.

182
00:06:13,553 --> 00:06:15,666
They let anybody in here.

183
00:06:15,846 --> 00:06:18,288
Then she turned to Evelyn and said,

184
00:06:18,288 --> 00:06:20,381
people like you should be at a

185
00:06:20,381 --> 00:06:23,172
shelter, not bothering people at dinner.

186
00:06:23,352 --> 00:06:25,105
Don't you have any shame?

187
00:06:25,455 --> 00:06:27,551
I watched Michael's face,

188
00:06:27,551 --> 00:06:28,473
sweetheart.

189
00:06:28,653 --> 00:06:30,267
I watched it break.

190
00:06:30,447 --> 00:06:32,641
And then Brittany did the thing I've

191
00:06:32,641 --> 00:06:33,617
never forgotten.

192
00:06:33,797 --> 00:06:36,196
She picked up the dinner roll from

193
00:06:36,196 --> 00:06:37,325
her bread plate,

194
00:06:37,325 --> 00:06:39,512
the one she'd complained about,

195
00:06:39,512 --> 00:06:41,558
and she held it out to Evelyn

196
00:06:41,558 --> 00:06:42,970
between two fingers,

197
00:06:42,970 --> 00:06:45,369
like you'd hold something out to a

198
00:06:45,369 --> 00:06:47,062
stray dog, and she said,

199
00:06:47,062 --> 00:06:47,415
here.

200
00:06:47,595 --> 00:06:48,710
Now go.

201
00:06:49,060 --> 00:06:50,801
Evelyn took the roll.

202
00:06:50,981 --> 00:06:52,653
She said, thank you,

203
00:06:52,653 --> 00:06:53,071
dear.

204
00:06:53,251 --> 00:06:54,609
God bless you.

205
00:06:54,789 --> 00:06:57,460
And she turned and shuffled out the

206
00:06:57,460 --> 00:06:59,445
door, back into the sleet.

207
00:06:59,625 --> 00:07:02,591
The waiter, a young man named Carlos,

208
00:07:02,591 --> 00:07:04,996
ran out after her with his own

209
00:07:04,996 --> 00:07:07,080
coat and a bowl of soup in

210
00:07:07,080 --> 00:07:08,042
a to-go cup.

211
00:07:08,222 --> 00:07:10,182
I saw him through the window,

212
00:07:10,182 --> 00:07:12,750
putting his coat around her shoulders.

213
00:07:12,930 --> 00:07:15,055
Remember Carlos, honey.

214
00:07:15,235 --> 00:07:16,628
He comes back.

215
00:07:16,978 --> 00:07:19,237
I found Evelyn around the corner,

216
00:07:19,237 --> 00:07:21,496
sitting in my car with the heater

217
00:07:21,496 --> 00:07:24,234
running, still holding that dinner roll.

218
00:07:24,414 --> 00:07:25,970
She wasn't crying.

219
00:07:26,150 --> 00:07:28,158
That's what scared me.

220
00:07:28,338 --> 00:07:30,653
She just sat there and said,

221
00:07:30,653 --> 00:07:31,728
well, Ruthie.

222
00:07:31,908 --> 00:07:33,127
Now I know.

223
00:07:33,307 --> 00:07:34,554
And then she said,

224
00:07:34,554 --> 00:07:36,909
the worst part isn't what she said

225
00:07:36,909 --> 00:07:37,324
to me.

226
00:07:37,504 --> 00:07:39,909
It's that Michael is going to have

227
00:07:39,909 --> 00:07:40,616
to choose.

228
00:07:40,796 --> 00:07:43,014
And I raised him to be kind,

229
00:07:43,014 --> 00:07:44,360
not to be strong.

230
00:07:44,710 --> 00:07:46,394
So far, the plan,

231
00:07:46,394 --> 00:07:49,168
the dinner, the dinner roll,

232
00:07:49,168 --> 00:07:50,654
and the waiter.

233
00:07:50,834 --> 00:07:53,899
Now here's what everybody asks me.

234
00:07:54,079 --> 00:07:55,553
What did Michael do?

235
00:07:55,733 --> 00:07:58,436
Because he didn't say anything at that

236
00:07:58,436 --> 00:07:59,716
table, sweetheart.

237
00:07:59,896 --> 00:08:02,283
He just sat there and finished the

238
00:08:02,283 --> 00:08:02,775
dinner.

239
00:08:02,955 --> 00:08:04,325
He paid.

240
00:08:04,505 --> 00:08:06,339
He drove Brittany home.

241
00:08:06,519 --> 00:08:09,115
And Evelyn didn't hear a word from

242
00:08:09,115 --> 00:08:10,490
him for nine days.

243
00:08:10,670 --> 00:08:13,262
Nine days, and the wedding was set

244
00:08:13,262 --> 00:08:14,710
for New Year's Eve.

245
00:08:15,060 --> 00:08:17,766
Those nine days were the longest of

246
00:08:17,766 --> 00:08:19,390
Evelyn's life, honey.

247
00:08:19,570 --> 00:08:20,789
She didn't sleep.

248
00:08:20,969 --> 00:08:23,549
She called me every night at eleven

249
00:08:23,549 --> 00:08:24,139
o'clock.

250
00:08:24,319 --> 00:08:27,062
She said, what if I've lost him,

251
00:08:27,062 --> 00:08:27,662
Ruthie?

252
00:08:27,842 --> 00:08:29,868
What if he's angry at me and

253
00:08:29,868 --> 00:08:30,664
not at her?

254
00:08:30,844 --> 00:08:33,039
What if he marries her anyway,

255
00:08:33,039 --> 00:08:34,211
just to show me?

256
00:08:34,391 --> 00:08:37,437
I'd rather lose every bakery I own

257
00:08:37,437 --> 00:08:39,139
than lose that boy.

258
00:08:39,319 --> 00:08:41,669
And for the first time in sixty

259
00:08:41,669 --> 00:08:44,323
years, I heard Evelyn sound afraid.

260
00:08:44,673 --> 00:08:46,902
Evelyn thought the wedding was off.

261
00:08:47,082 --> 00:08:49,276
Then the invitation came.

262
00:08:49,456 --> 00:08:50,697
White and gold,

263
00:08:50,697 --> 00:08:52,435
three hundred guests,

264
00:08:52,435 --> 00:08:55,414
at the biggest church in Cincinnati,

265
00:08:55,414 --> 00:08:57,897
paid for by Brittany's father.

266
00:08:58,077 --> 00:08:59,502
And on the back,

267
00:08:59,502 --> 00:09:01,728
in Michael's handwriting,

268
00:09:01,728 --> 00:09:03,242
it said, Grandma,

269
00:09:03,242 --> 00:09:04,311
please come.

270
00:09:04,491 --> 00:09:06,279
Wear your best dress.

271
00:09:06,459 --> 00:09:07,434
Trust me.

272
00:09:07,614 --> 00:09:09,805
Evelyn called me and said,

273
00:09:09,805 --> 00:09:12,839
Ruthie, I don't understand that boy.

274
00:09:13,019 --> 00:09:14,021
And I said,

275
00:09:14,021 --> 00:09:15,387
I think you do.

276
00:09:15,737 --> 00:09:17,155
On New Year's Eve,

277
00:09:17,155 --> 00:09:19,520
Evelyn and I sat in the second

278
00:09:19,520 --> 00:09:19,835
row.

279
00:09:20,015 --> 00:09:22,771
She wore her navy blue church dress

280
00:09:22,771 --> 00:09:23,637
from Sears.

281
00:09:23,817 --> 00:09:26,675
Brittany's mother looked her up and down

282
00:09:26,675 --> 00:09:28,747
and asked if she was with the

283
00:09:28,747 --> 00:09:29,390
caterers.

284
00:09:29,570 --> 00:09:32,051
The church was full of flowers and

285
00:09:32,051 --> 00:09:32,635
candles.

286
00:09:32,815 --> 00:09:35,074
Brittany came down the aisle in a

287
00:09:35,074 --> 00:09:37,471
dress that cost more than my house.

288
00:09:37,651 --> 00:09:39,855
And Michael stood at the front,

289
00:09:39,855 --> 00:09:41,064
white as a sheet.

290
00:09:41,414 --> 00:09:44,297
When the minister asked if anybody had

291
00:09:44,297 --> 00:09:46,725
a reason these two should not be

292
00:09:46,725 --> 00:09:49,077
married, the church went quiet,

293
00:09:49,077 --> 00:09:50,822
the way it always does,

294
00:09:50,822 --> 00:09:52,188
for just a second.

295
00:09:52,368 --> 00:09:54,171
And Michael said,

296
00:09:54,171 --> 00:09:54,701
I do.

297
00:09:54,881 --> 00:09:57,087
Three hundred people gasped.

298
00:09:57,267 --> 00:09:59,736
Brittany laughed nervously and said,

299
00:09:59,736 --> 00:10:01,656
Michael, what are you doing?

300
00:10:01,836 --> 00:10:03,513
And Michael turned around,

301
00:10:03,513 --> 00:10:05,966
and he looked straight down the aisle,

302
00:10:05,966 --> 00:10:07,966
at the back door of the church.

303
00:10:08,316 --> 00:10:10,784
And through the back door came a

304
00:10:10,784 --> 00:10:13,252
little old woman in a torn brown

305
00:10:13,252 --> 00:10:15,411
coat, a scarf over her hair,

306
00:10:15,411 --> 00:10:16,953
and wet men's boots.

307
00:10:17,133 --> 00:10:18,382
My heart stopped,

308
00:10:18,382 --> 00:10:21,615
honey, because Evelyn was sitting right next

309
00:10:21,615 --> 00:10:22,056
to me.

310
00:10:22,236 --> 00:10:23,722
It wasn't Evelyn.

311
00:10:23,902 --> 00:10:26,787
It was a woman from the shelter

312
00:10:26,787 --> 00:10:28,368
on Fourth Street,

313
00:10:28,368 --> 00:10:29,392
a real one,

314
00:10:29,392 --> 00:10:30,322
named Mrs.

315
00:10:30,502 --> 00:10:33,661
Lottie Brown, and she walked slowly up

316
00:10:33,661 --> 00:10:34,991
that long aisle,

317
00:10:34,991 --> 00:10:37,817
while three hundred people stared.

318
00:10:38,167 --> 00:10:39,910
Michael said, Brittany,

319
00:10:39,910 --> 00:10:40,970
two weeks ago,

320
00:10:40,970 --> 00:10:43,547
a woman dressed like this asked to

321
00:10:43,547 --> 00:10:45,972
sit at our table for one minute,

322
00:10:45,972 --> 00:10:48,548
and you called her trash and threw

323
00:10:48,548 --> 00:10:49,382
her a roll.

324
00:10:49,562 --> 00:10:50,676
This is Mrs.

325
00:10:50,856 --> 00:10:51,716
Brown.

326
00:10:51,896 --> 00:10:54,381
She's lived on the street for six

327
00:10:54,381 --> 00:10:54,833
years.

328
00:10:55,013 --> 00:10:57,688
I've been bringing her dinner every night

329
00:10:57,688 --> 00:10:58,798
since that night,

330
00:10:58,798 --> 00:11:00,690
because somebody should have.

331
00:11:00,870 --> 00:11:01,856
Then he said,

332
00:11:01,856 --> 00:11:04,132
and the woman at our table was

333
00:11:04,132 --> 00:11:05,270
my grandmother.

334
00:11:05,621 --> 00:11:07,815
And he pointed right at Evelyn.

335
00:11:07,995 --> 00:11:09,841
Everybody turned around.

336
00:11:10,021 --> 00:11:13,319
Brittany's mother, the one who'd asked about

337
00:11:13,319 --> 00:11:15,118
the caterers, went pale.

338
00:11:15,298 --> 00:11:19,628
Michael said, my grandmother owns Evelyn's Bakeries.

339
00:11:19,808 --> 00:11:21,619
All forty-two of them.

340
00:11:21,799 --> 00:11:23,018
I never told you,

341
00:11:23,018 --> 00:11:25,743
because I wanted somebody who loved me

342
00:11:25,743 --> 00:11:26,676
with nothing.

343
00:11:26,856 --> 00:11:28,864
And now I know you don't.

344
00:11:29,044 --> 00:11:30,228
I'm sorry.

345
00:11:30,408 --> 00:11:32,011
I can't marry you.

346
00:11:32,191 --> 00:11:34,836
Then he walked down the aisle and

347
00:11:34,836 --> 00:11:35,557
took Mrs.

348
00:11:35,737 --> 00:11:36,875
Brown's arm.

349
00:11:37,225 --> 00:11:39,303
Brittany screamed, honey.

350
00:11:39,483 --> 00:11:41,826
She screamed that it was a trick,

351
00:11:41,826 --> 00:11:43,531
and that it wasn't fair,

352
00:11:43,531 --> 00:11:45,803
and that she'd have been nice if

353
00:11:45,803 --> 00:11:46,797
she had known.

354
00:11:46,977 --> 00:11:49,161
And that was the whole point,

355
00:11:49,161 --> 00:11:49,914
wasn't it?

356
00:11:50,094 --> 00:11:52,364
She would have been nice if she'd

357
00:11:52,364 --> 00:11:52,776
known.

358
00:11:52,956 --> 00:11:55,046
Her father had to walk her out

359
00:11:55,046 --> 00:11:56,021
the side door.

360
00:11:56,201 --> 00:11:59,551
The three hundred guests were still standing

361
00:11:59,551 --> 00:12:02,291
there, and Evelyn stood up and said,

362
00:12:02,291 --> 00:12:04,270
well, the food's paid for.

363
00:12:04,450 --> 00:12:05,472
Let's eat.

364
00:12:05,822 --> 00:12:08,852
Michael didn't marry for four more years.

365
00:12:09,032 --> 00:12:10,293
And when he did,

366
00:12:10,293 --> 00:12:12,895
it was a girl he met volunteering

367
00:12:12,895 --> 00:12:15,891
at that same shelter on Fourth Street,

368
00:12:15,891 --> 00:12:17,310
a nurse named Ana,

369
00:12:17,310 --> 00:12:20,700
whose family came from Mexico with nothing.

370
00:12:20,880 --> 00:12:23,221
The first time she met Evelyn,

371
00:12:23,221 --> 00:12:25,875
Evelyn wore her torn brown coat on

372
00:12:25,875 --> 00:12:26,499
purpose.

373
00:12:26,679 --> 00:12:28,628
Ana took one look at her,

374
00:12:28,628 --> 00:12:30,421
took off her own scarf,

375
00:12:30,421 --> 00:12:33,227
and wrapped it around Evelyn's neck.

376
00:12:33,577 --> 00:12:35,287
And Carlos, the waiter,

377
00:12:35,287 --> 00:12:37,221
the one who ran out in the

378
00:12:37,221 --> 00:12:38,708
sleet with his coat?

379
00:12:38,888 --> 00:12:41,404
Evelyn found him the week after the

380
00:12:41,404 --> 00:12:41,907
dinner.

381
00:12:42,087 --> 00:12:46,442
Today, sweetheart, Carlos runs eleven of Evelyn's

382
00:12:46,442 --> 00:12:47,242
bakeries.

383
00:12:47,422 --> 00:12:48,362
Mrs.

384
00:12:48,542 --> 00:12:51,291
Lottie Brown lived the last eight years

385
00:12:51,291 --> 00:12:53,617
of her life in a little apartment

386
00:12:53,617 --> 00:12:55,520
above the Mansfield bakery,

387
00:12:55,520 --> 00:12:58,339
rent free, and she frosted the Christmas

388
00:12:58,339 --> 00:13:01,441
cookies every December until she was ninety.

389
00:13:01,791 --> 00:13:04,531
Evelyn passed in twenty fourteen.

390
00:13:04,711 --> 00:13:05,752
At her funeral,

391
00:13:05,752 --> 00:13:07,836
Michael told that whole story,

392
00:13:07,836 --> 00:13:08,669
and he said,

393
00:13:08,669 --> 00:13:11,309
my grandmother taught me that you find

394
00:13:11,309 --> 00:13:13,392
out who someone is by how they

395
00:13:13,392 --> 00:13:15,684
treat a person who can do nothing

396
00:13:15,684 --> 00:13:16,309
for them.

397
00:13:16,489 --> 00:13:19,296
I've thought about that every day since,

398
00:13:19,296 --> 00:13:19,717
honey.

399
00:13:19,897 --> 00:13:22,184
Not how people treat the boss.

400
00:13:22,364 --> 00:13:24,311
How they treat the waiter,

401
00:13:24,311 --> 00:13:25,659
the cleaning lady,

402
00:13:25,659 --> 00:13:27,681
the old woman in wet boots.

403
00:13:28,031 --> 00:13:29,894
Tell me in the comments,

404
00:13:29,894 --> 00:13:30,747
sweetheart.

405
00:13:30,927 --> 00:13:33,374
Was Evelyn right to test her,

406
00:13:33,374 --> 00:13:35,061
or was it too cruel?

407
00:13:35,241 --> 00:13:37,203
Be honest with Grandma.

408
00:13:37,383 --> 00:13:39,658
I go back and forth myself.

409
00:13:39,838 --> 00:13:42,205
There are more of my family's stories

410
00:13:42,205 --> 00:13:44,443
in the playlist right there on your

411
00:13:44,443 --> 00:13:46,426
screen, and I'll see you in the

412
00:13:46,426 --> 00:13:47,002
next one.

413
00:13:47,182 --> 00:13:48,842
Good night, honey.
